<main>

<!-- ===================== SUMMARY ===================== -->
<section id="summary">
  <h2>Summary <small>what Arcana is and how it runs here</small></h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>Arcana turns human intent into <em>verified</em> runtime behaviour. A change is elicited into a formal contract, proven against a monitored substrate, and promoted only when its proof obligations are discharged. Every guarantee has one shape:</p>
    <p class="callout" style="margin-top:0"><strong>if</strong> module ⊨ contract C <strong>and</strong> substrate ⊨ contract-set S, <strong>then</strong> the domain goal G holds. The substrate (BEAM/OTP plus layers L0–L1) is <em>assumed and monitored</em>; the business logic built on it is <em>proven</em>.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:0.7rem 0 0;font-size:0.82rem">Source: <span class="mono">PURPOSE.md</span>, <span class="mono">DESIGN.md</span> and <span class="mono">docs/proof-driven/</span> in the arcana2 repo. This is a ground-up rewrite of Arcana v1 (retired).</p>
  </div>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="widget k-app">
      <div class="w-label">Runtime</div>
      <div class="w-value">2 <small>clustered dev nodes</small></div>
      <div class="w-sub"><span class="mono">arcana@arcana-dev</span> (primary) · <span class="mono">arcana@arcana-dev-2</span> (follower)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="widget k-net">
      <div class="w-label">Admin console</div>
      <div class="w-value"><a href="https://{{ tailscale_hostname }}:{{ arcana2_nginx_port }}">:{{ arcana2_nginx_port }}</a></div>
      <div class="w-sub">nginx TLS → 127.0.0.1:{{ arcana2_port }} · chat, registry, journal, requirements</div>
    </div>
    <div class="widget k-data">
      <div class="w-label">Database</div>
      <div class="w-value"><span class="mono">arcana_dev</span></div>
      <div class="w-sub">YugabyteDB YSQL on homelab-net; one <span class="mono">arcana_test_*</span> database per worktree</div>
    </div>
    <div class="widget k-gpu">
      <div class="w-label">Proof toolchain</div>
      <div class="w-value">Lean · F* · Z3</div>
      <div class="w-sub">warm daemons in the dev image; WASM kernels run on wasmtime</div>
    </div>
    <div class="widget k-sys">
      <div class="w-label">Code size <span class="muted">(snapshot)</span></div>
      <div class="w-value">25 <small>boot subsystems incl. Web</small></div>
      <div class="w-sub">~230 Elixir source files under <span class="mono">lib/arcana</span>: core 68, state 37, web 32, spec 16</div>
    </div>
{% if arcana_summary | length > 0 %}
{{ arcana_summary }}
{% endif %}
  </div>
{% if arcana_summary | length == 0 %}
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:0.7rem;font-size:0.8rem">Live status tiles (migrations, proof state, queue depth …) appear here once <code>overview-summary.html</code> exists in the arcana2 repo — see <a href="#contributed">From the Arcana repo</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

