<!-- ===================== PIPELINE ===================== -->
<section id="pipeline">
  <h2>Intent → proof → running kernel <small>how the subsystems are used together</small></h2>
  <div class="card">
  <div class="diagram">
<svg viewBox="0 0 1200 170" role="img" aria-label="Pipeline from intent through elicitation, specification, verification, registry promotion and kernel execution to the journal and conformance monitors">
  <defs>
    <marker id="a-pipe" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" class="ah"/></marker>
  </defs>
  <rect class="node k-ext" x="16" y="40" width="148" height="90" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="28" y="64">Intent</text><text class="s" x="28" y="84">natural language</text><text class="s" x="28" y="100">human goal</text>
  <rect class="node k-app" x="186" y="40" width="148" height="90" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="198" y="64">Arcana.Elicit</text><text class="s" x="198" y="84">ReqNode graph</text><text class="s" x="198" y="100">LLM untrusted</text>
  <rect class="node k-gpu" x="356" y="40" width="148" height="90" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="368" y="64">Arcana.Spec</text><text class="s" x="368" y="84">Lean IR + ontology</text><text class="s" x="368" y="100">content-addressed</text>
  <rect class="node k-gpu" x="526" y="40" width="148" height="90" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="538" y="64">Arcana.Verify</text><text class="s" x="538" y="84">Lean · F* · Z3 certs</text><text class="s" x="538" y="100">ProofCache</text>
  <rect class="node k-gpu" x="696" y="40" width="148" height="90" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="708" y="64">Code.Registry</text><text class="s" x="708" y="84">promote on discharge</text><text class="s" x="708" y="100">pointer-swap rollout</text>
  <rect class="node k-gpu" x="866" y="40" width="148" height="90" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="878" y="64">Kernel + Executor</text><text class="s" x="878" y="84">WASM kernel emits plan</text><text class="s" x="878" y="100">executor runs effects</text>
  <rect class="node k-data" x="1036" y="40" width="148" height="90" rx="8"/>
  <text class="t" x="1048" y="64">Journal · Monitors</text><text class="s" x="1048" y="84">gap-free replay oracle</text><text class="s" x="1048" y="100">assumptions monitored</text>
  <path class="edge" d="M164 85H186" marker-end="url(#a-pipe)"/><path class="edge" d="M334 85H356" marker-end="url(#a-pipe)"/>
  <path class="edge" d="M504 85H526" marker-end="url(#a-pipe)"/><path class="edge" d="M674 85H696" marker-end="url(#a-pipe)"/>
  <path class="edge" d="M844 85H866" marker-end="url(#a-pipe)"/><path class="edge" d="M1014 85H1036" marker-end="url(#a-pipe)"/>
  <text class="z" x="186" y="24">LLM translates</text>
  <text class="z" x="356" y="24">non-LLM gates</text>
  <text class="z" x="866" y="24">capability-bound effects</text>
</svg>
  </div>
  <p class="muted" style="margin:0.8rem 0 0;font-size:0.82rem">The LLM only translates; every output passes a non-LLM gate before it can be promoted. A change that cannot be proven cannot promote, and the journal makes “verified to contract” checkable by byte-exact replay. In the admin console this is the chat workflow: intent → goal → routine → Lean discharge → proof-carrying plan.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== DEVELOPMENT ===================== -->
<section id="development">
  <h2>Development <small>Claude Code and MCP against the live cluster</small></h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Workflow</h3>
      <p class="muted" style="font-size:0.85rem">Claude Code edits the bind-mounted checkout, the primary recompiles on save, and MCP lets the session inspect and drive the live nodes. The diagram is on the <a href="/overview.html#arcana-dev">homelab overview</a>.</p>
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Start / stop</dt><dd class="mono">make dev.up · make dev.down</dd>
        <dt>Cluster view</dt><dd class="mono">make dev.cluster · make dev.logs</dd>
        <dt>REPL</dt><dd class="mono">make dev.iex (remsh to the primary)</dd>
        <dt>Checks</dt><dd class="mono">docker exec arcana-dev make check</dd>
        <dt>Worktrees</dt><dd class="mono">.worktrees/&lt;subsystem&gt;, one DB each</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>MCP tools</h3>
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Tidewave</dt><dd class="mono">/tidewave/mcp: project_eval, get_docs, get_logs, get_source_location, execute_sql_query</dd>
        <dt>Read</dt><dd class="mono">arcana_status, registry_list/get, artifact, journal_read, model, logs</dd>
        <dt>Mutating</dt><dd class="mono">arcana_lifecycle, arcana_kernel_step, arcana_conformance_reset</dd>
        <dt>Audit</dt><dd>every mutating call lands in journal stream <span class="mono">dev_mcp:audit</span></dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== RUNTIME ===================== -->
<section id="runtime">
  <h2>Runtime wiring <small>owned by the homelab</small></h2>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
      <dl class="kv">
        <dt>Source</dt><dd class="mono">{{ arcana2_src_path }} (bind-mounted at /workspace)</dd>
        <dt>Containers</dt><dd class="mono">arcana-dev :4100, arcana-dev-2 :4101</dd>
        <dt>Ports</dt><dd>127.0.0.1 plus the tailnet IP, never all interfaces</dd>
        <dt>Console</dt><dd><a href="https://{{ tailscale_hostname }}:{{ arcana2_nginx_port }}">https://{{ tailscale_hostname }}:{{ arcana2_nginx_port }}</a></dd>
        <dt>Clustering</dt><dd>libcluster Epmd over <span class="mono">ARCANA_CLUSTER_HOSTS</span>, shared cookie</dd>
        <dt>Database</dt><dd><span class="mono">arcana_dev</span> on YugabyteDB; only the primary runs migrations</dd>
        <dt>LLM</dt><dd>Anthropic API (key in a root-only env file)</dd>
        <dt>Playbook</dt><dd class="mono">playbooks/arcana2.yml</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Notes</h3>
      <ul style="margin:0;padding-left:1.1rem;font-size:0.85rem">
        <li>The nodes are <span class="mono">restart: unless-stopped</span>; the follower waits for the primary's health check.</li>
        <li>Per-node state (ETS, log ring buffer, memory store) is not shared; durable state is the database plus the local store root.</li>
        <li>Durable guarantees depend on YugabyteDB. It is the homelab's only SQL database, loopback-only with auth off.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

